WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.060
Are you sure Yuta came down here?

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.150
I definitely saw him.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.610
He wandered down this way.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.840
What a pain.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.740
If we can't find him, 
let's leave without him.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.160
I'm pretty sure he turned this...

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.820
There he is!

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.010
Yuta...

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.410
I love you!

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.670
Please go out with me.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.670
There's no way—

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.670
Hey, everyone.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.750
So there you are.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.470
What?

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.350
Huh? Is that...

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.170
Who is she? Is she a first year?

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.010
She's our year. I think 
her name's Takahashi-san.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.280
We shouldn't be spying on them.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.900
We should go talk to her.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.950
No.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.700
It'll be fine as long 
as they don't find out.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.030
That's not the issue.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:01.810
Oh.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:02.600
What?

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.400
Yuta's coming this way.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:49.140
So hot.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.350
So cool.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.730
How can it be this hot?

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.160
September's already over.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.140
I can't believe we're changing 
 to our winter uniforms soon.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.570
I know.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:06.610
Imagine how I feel, bathing in
 sweat every time I take a nap.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:07.870
That's not possible.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.710
Okay, let's trade.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.910
Got it! This time...

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.840
Come on. Rock, paper, scissors...

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:20.640
Shoot!

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.010
I lost again!

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:22.670
Three losses in a row.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.220
Hurry up.

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.720
So hot.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.660
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot...

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.510
Can't you even shut up for a little bit?

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.370
But it's so hot!

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.770
Looks like the heat's getting to them.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:41.640
Super-ultra-executive-angelic-super hot.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.500
Kaname's like that all year round.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.990
It only feels hotter 'cause you won't shut up about it.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.990
Anyway...

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.870
Maybe this sausage fest's making us feel the heat more.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.810
Y-You're right. That must be it.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.830
We're all second years.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.770
We should have one or two...

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.260
or maybe even three or four 
girlfriends by now, if that's your preference.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.220
If it's our preference, you say...

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:11.520
Out of five of us, one might already have a girlfriend.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.730
Maybe... one of us...

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:19.710
I don't feel a breeze. Fan me.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:22.970
What?

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:24.110
Nothing.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.940
He's not going to talk about it?

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.140
That must not have been a confession.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.110
They were rehearsing for 
a play or something.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.840
That's ridiculous.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.330
Yuki, did he say anything to you?

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:40.210
No, and I tell Yuta everything.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.160
We're not talking about your 
relationship with Yuta here.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.840
Oh, that reminds me.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.140
Yesterday...

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.270
Yesterday?

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:49.400
Co...

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.390
Co...

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.850
Could any of you have taken my 
dictionary out of my locker?

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.370
You guys seemed awfully interested just now.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.020
Yuta.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.440
I might as well ask since 
I have the opportunity.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.400
Yesterday, co...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.990
Could someone have 
taken your dictionary?

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.160
Stupid! You're just plain stupid!

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:16.720
I feel juice tastes different from 
a cup than from a can.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.880
Maybe it's the ice. Maybe it's the straw.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.520
Or maybe it's just my imagination.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.670
But the biggest reason

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.220
is because of this sound.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:37.190
Next to an Apple

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.270
Is Yutan really not going to tell us?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.310
Maybe he rejected her 
when she asked him out.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:47.390
That could be it.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:54.480
No one would turn down a date.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.210
Not even I've done that.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.470
Chizuru, I bet no one's ever 
confessed their feelings for you.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.760
What did you say?!

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.500
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:03.840
Calm down.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.390
Yutan, Shun-chan, let's go.

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:09.620
O-Okay.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.000
Yutan, let's go.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.950
Actually, um...

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:19.060
I can't go home with you guys today.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.860
I have something to do.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.060
Something to do?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.070
Something to do.

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.070
Well, guys, shall we go?

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.080
Sure.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.700
Yutan, see you later.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.690
See you later.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.720
What do we do? What do 
we do? What do we do?

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:39.730
What do we do?

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.710
You're asking me what we should do?

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.590
They must be meeting up somewhere.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.920
Normally it'd be at the front entrance.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:52.000
Let's split up and meet up again down 
there, so Yuta doesn't suspect anything.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.050
Roger.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:53.700
Roger.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:54.580
R-Roger.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:03.680
Takahashi-san.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:06.790
Sorry. Were you waiting long?

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:08.070
Not at all.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.610
An after-school date.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.320
He should at least tell 
us if he's dating her.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.990
I'd never accept it, though.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:18.640
They're leaving. Come on, come on.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:21.470
Wh-What? We're going to follow them?

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:23.070
We really shouldn't be doing this.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.500
We can't let him out of our sight 
if he's keeping it secret.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.170
Now, let's...

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.590
Keep it down.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:34.010
Sorry. I'm just so young and eager.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:37.440
You too.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.560
You can't just walk out 
in the open like that.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.730
They're gone.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.590
Oh snap. Which way did they go?

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:47.160
What are we gonna do? We lost them.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.530
Um...

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:52.660
I think they probably went down those stairs.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.290
Shun, you're curious, too?

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.430
Don't push me.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:06.710
Take this seriously or we'll be found out.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.540
What do you mean, seriously?

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.710
Isn't tailing them wrong 
in the first place?

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.520
<i>So they did follow us.</i>

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.300
<i>They must have nothing else to do.</i>

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.090
E-Excuse me.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.020
Nothing.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.850
Are you tired from the heat?

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.970
What? No, I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.230
Do you want to go somewhere?

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.270
Oh, u-um...

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.820
How about the bookstore?

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.050
The bookstore?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.130
Let's do that, then.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:41.290
Where's the closest one to here?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.290
Closest to here? Probably...

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:48.360
<i>When he asked if I 
wanted to go somewhere...</i>

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.010
Hey, Squadsman Yukki.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:58.600
Come back. Don't go over there.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.650
The bookstore.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.020
How unexpected.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:05.520
<b>"Next to an Apple"</b>

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:04.040
Sorry about suggesting the bookstore.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.520
Is there something you wanna get here?

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:06.730
Yes.

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:12.760
I'll go buy this.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:13.400
Wait.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.270
Don't you hate getting the top one?

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.160
Not that I'd ever buy this.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.340
My brother's got some strange habits.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:28.670
If there's only one copy left, 
he'll go to another store.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:34.670
I'm sure you don't care about that, though.

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:38.930
What should we do?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.450
Everything seems to be 
progressing smoothly.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:46.670
There's no rush. We're 
still glass pistols.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:48.900
Cracks can form so easily.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.440
But Yutan's not making any mistakes.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.980
Well, it is Yuta after all...

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.070
So, which one of you did that?

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.920
Shun, how rude.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:02.780
You shouldn't do that, Shun-chan.

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.950
What? I-I didn't do anything.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.160
Who did it?!

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.030
<i>How long are they going to follow me?</i>

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:15.530
You like books?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.370
Yes.

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:20.930
I end up reading all day on days off.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:24.180
Yuta-kun, what do you do on days off?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.290
Me?

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.450
I dunno...

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:32.160
Listen to CDs, go shopping 
with my brother,

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.110
watch my brother play video games.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:38.720
I don't really do anything.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:41.240
All I do is read.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:45.480
I go to the bookstore and the library.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.940
I'm sorry I'm not more interesting.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:51.130
Why? What's wrong with that?

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:52.800
You have something you love doing.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.660
Unlike Yuki, I don't really have anything like that.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.400
I said I listen to CDs, but I only have

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.340
the one I bought because I liked the cover.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:04.950
It's not even that great, so 
I don't listen to it much.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.350
Oh, but...

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:12.420
I like books, but I don't 
like every book I own.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.730
I've got a bunch I've only read once.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:19.240
And I don't think it's 
bad to only own one CD.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:25.070
Oh, I'm sorry, I just...

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:30.040
Sorry.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:42.090
I'll lend you that CD sometime.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.280
Okay.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:52.130
Shun-chan, write a text we can send to Yutan.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.610
What? Let's not do this.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:56.950
Yuta's always got his phone on silent,

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:59.230
so he'll ignore all the 
messages we send him.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.550
Then the text bombing plan won't work.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:06.240
The enemy's a tough one, 
Squadsman Shun-chan.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.940
The enemy?

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:11.180
Why can't we just be happy 
for him like normal people?

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:15.250
It's sad he didn't tell us about it,

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.340
but we should be happy that 
our friend has found love.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:19.190
Love?

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:21.390
You're saying Yutan likes that girl?

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:24.620
That's the first I've heard of it.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.180
What? But if he doesn't, why 
would he go out with her?

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:32.690
Some people go out with people 
they don't have feelings for.

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:35.160
What are you doing with your hands?

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:39.690
I guess, but I wonder 
what Yuta's thinking.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:43.830
The only way to know is to eavesdrop.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.310
We can throw a paper cup phone in...

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:48.390
That would bother the other customers.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:49.700
He was just kidding.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:54.960
Hush, you really are bothering people.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.000
How long have you been there?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.110
How long are you going to follow me?

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:01.000
H-Have you known the whole time?

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.210
It was obvious.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:04.950
Where's your girlfriend?

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:07.470
Takahashi-san? She went home.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.560
Why didn't you go with her?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.200
Aren't you dating?

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:16.710
Could it be you don't like her, Yutan?

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.390
But you accepted her confession anyway,

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:20.110
which is why you couldn't tell us?

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.800
Chizuru-kun, don't say that.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.820
Well, Yutan?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:26.860
Um...

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.170
Your fries.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.990
What a waste.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:34.250
Chizuru-kun, don't eat 
things off the floor.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:48.970
Um...

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.020
Hold the other side.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.400
I felt relieved when I heard his voice.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.400
But also nervous.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.820
Are you okay?

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.420
I'm...

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:11.700
You're?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.370
I'm fine.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:18.670
But I never planned 
on confessing to him.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.240
How'd it go with Yuta-kun?

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:22.800
Huh?

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:27.490
You finally asked him out? I was
 wondering when you would.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:28.700
Me too.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.760
We went out for tea the other day.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:36.520
What? But Takahashi, you're 
terrible at making conversation.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.490
Did you just drink in silence?

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:41.030
Did you just look at your 
phones the whole time?

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:43.240
You have to try to talk 
to him.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.900
Takahashi, you're too shy.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:50.030
Yuta-kun's pretty talkative.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:54.490
He's nice. I had fun.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.040
I see.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.000
Th-That's great.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:03.030
By the way, I started playing 
Taiko drums recently.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.060
Taiko?

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:05.990
It's actually pretty fun.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.810
Takahashi, is something wrong?

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:08.510
No.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.440
We've got contemporary literature next.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.720
I need to borrow a textbook.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.020
Me too.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:17.900
What? You forgot yours, Jun-chan?

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:19.750
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.100
Me too.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:21.940
Really? You wanna come with?

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:22.920
Sure.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:29.630
Here's the CD I said I'd lend you.

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:31.750
Thank—

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:34.670
It's Wednesday. Contemporary 
literature's on Thursday.

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:37.030
Jun-chan, you were freaking out, too.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:39.380
Th-Thanks.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:41.220
The sixth track's pretty good.

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:43.460
It's a bit like a ballad, but I like it.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.190
Jun-chan, over here.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.320
What?

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:47.210
Hurry up.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:48.230
What is it?

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:48.960
Just hurry.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:52.490
Any songs on it you recommend?

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:56.340
What? Yeah, the sixth track...

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:58.220
I see. I look forward 
to listening to it.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:00.230
There's a crack in it.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:03.560
I'm so sorry. I'll buy you 
a new one. I'm sorry.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.580
It's fine. It's not 
like the CD inside broke.

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:08.460
But... But...

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.490
It's...

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.490
It's okay.

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:26.600
Sorry I'm late.

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:27.210
Don't sweat it.

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:29.090
What about your friends?

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:29.710
What?

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:34.040
Oh, they've already gone home.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.000
Everything's going smoothly, 
Squadsman Shun-chan.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.970
Let's stop this already.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:42.800
You're spying on them, too.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.520
Let's go.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.310
What?

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.580
Let's just go.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.440
The CD...

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.990
What? I'm sorry! I'll replace it.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.280
That's not what I meant.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:58.490
When you return it, you can 
just put it in my locker.

00:16:58.900 --> 00:16:59.700
What?

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:07.800
I never thought Takahashi 
would pull this off.

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:11.560
What? You're regretting it now?

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.340
You're the one who told her to confess.

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:17.980
I was kidding. I didn't 
think she'd actually do it.

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:19.390
We're talking about Yuta-kun.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:23.350
You thought he'd reject 
her. You're awful.

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:27.500
I was convinced he'd 
turn her down, too.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:28.660
I know, right?

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:32.280
Takahashi-san.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.620
Let's wait a bit before we go.

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:39.330
That was when I realized...

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:45.700
Yuta-kun always knew.

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.870
Why? Let's go.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.800
Takahashi, hurry.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:53.710
O-Okay.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:56.880
I could barely keep up with them.

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:59.360
Just tell him how you feel.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:02.420
I'm sure he'll say yes. You're really cute.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.170
I didn't want them to hate me.

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:13.780
I...

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:22.450
I look so stupid...

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:47.980
Sorry, Yuta-kun.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:52.520
Thank you for not rejecting me or...

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:58.070
Don't worry about it.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:08.040
I knew my friends were saying 
those things behind my back.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:17.590
It must sound pathetic, 
but I can't abandon them.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:18.890
Sure.

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:23.600
I'm scared to be alone.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:30.080
Besides, there are times I have fun being with them.

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:32.060
Yeah.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:42.910
You don't need to force 
yourself away from them.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:47.480
If you don't dislike them, 
you should stay with them.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:51.710
The CD—

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.530
Sorry, I'll replace it!

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.840
That's not what I was going to say.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:03.120
I think it grew on me.

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:06.510
I came to like it.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:10.090
I wouldn't say I love it yet, though.

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:14.330
I think if you change a little,

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:19.490
you might have more 
fun with your friends.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.710
You might even grow to like them.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:27.410
I think it'd be nice if that happened.

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:29.160
Yuta-kun.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:35.200
Sorry, that's all I can do for you.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:52.550
What? I have my own.

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:11.710
You broke up?

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:12.450
Yeah.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.410
That was quick. Why?

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:17.510
Because they couldn't handle 
the silence, obviously.

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:20.710
Love's not that simple.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.190
Where'd that come from?

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:24.930
Takahashi, you brat.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:29.350
Summer's ending.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:36.100
The cool autumn must be unbearable 
for the rejected, huh?

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:39.420
This wouldn't have happened

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:42.210
if you hadn't kept it secret from us.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:44.570
Remember that.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:46.250
Okay, okay.

00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:48.830
I'll buy you some juice 
to make up for it.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:50.060
Really?

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:54.280
I can only afford one though, 
so you'll have to share.

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:55.710
What?

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:00.830
Bam.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.620
Hey...

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:06.540
I almost experienced my 
first back pain just now.

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:07.800
I'll go with you.

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.420
No, you're too heavy.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.560
Who cares? It's a date.

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:20.480
Juice tastes different from 
a cup than from a can.

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:25.360
Maybe it's the ice. Maybe it's the straw.

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:27.820
Or maybe it's just my imagination.

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:29.910
<b>Asaba Yuta</b>

00:22:31.980 --> 00:22:36.090
But the biggest reason 
is because of this sound.

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:17.080
Next time: "Daily Wage Hero."

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:19.850
Daily Wage Hero/Senpai and Me

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:18.960
"Senpai and Me.
